    <string name="square_report_explanation_content">You should ensure that your complaint is made in good faith and represents your true intent. As a neutral platform service provider, SeekWeb4 will independently assess and handle your complaint as soon as possible in accordance with relevant international conventions, international digital service standards, and applicable laws and regulations.\n\nSeekWeb4 will take reasonable measures to protect your personal information. Except as required by laws and regulations, SeekWeb4 will not disclose your personal information to third parties without your permission.\n\nUnder relevant international conventions and digital copyright protection standards, rights holders must provide authentic identity information when notifying network service providers. Therefore, when you submit an infringement complaint or an impersonation complaint, we will collect relevant information (including sensitive personal information) based on your entity type, including your name or organization name, ID number or organization registration number, front and back photos of your ID, and company or organization certificate photos, for the purpose of verifying the authenticity of your identity. If you authorize an agent to file a complaint, we will also collect the agent\'s name, ID number, front and back photos of the ID, and a photo of the authorization letter to verify the agent\'s identity. You may refuse to provide this information; if you do, we may be unable to evaluate your complaint, but this will not affect your normal use of other SeekWeb4 features.\n\nIn addition, to evaluate your complaint, you should also provide relevant evidence that can be effectively submitted and is necessary for complaint assessment.\n\nIf SeekWeb4 has reasonable grounds to believe that a complaint falls under any of the following circumstances, it may adjust the handling method according to the actual situation, including but not limited to:\n(1) filing a complaint while knowing or should have known that it does not constitute infringement, or clearly lacking rights basis and factual grounds;\n(2) repeatedly filing complaints without substantive supplements after being informed that handling basis is insufficient;\n(3) submitting infringement complaints multiple times or in large volumes with a low overall approval rate or suspected abuse of complaints;\n(4) adversely affecting the platform\'s normal handling of other rights holders\' infringement complaints without reasonable and legitimate grounds;\n(5) other circumstances that SeekWeb4 has reason to believe are unreasonable or abusive complaints.\n\nOnce identified, special handling mechanisms or restriction measures may be applied, including but not limited to limiting frequency, adding to an abnormal complaint list, and adjusting the processing order of infringement complaint tickets, which may result in complaints not being submitted at high frequency, not being approved, or delayed review and assessment.\n\nIf the platform\'s processing capacity is overloaded due to special reasons, including but not limited to network factors, device issues, or a short-term surge in complaint volume, SeekWeb4\'s processing and feedback may also be adjusted or delayed.</string>
